Package: GiottoIngest
Title: Rust Ingest Backend for GiottoDisk Stores
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Ruben", "Dries", , "rdries@bu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Prototype Rust backend that reads spatial omics inputs fast
    and writes GiottoDisk point tile stores, reproducing the R writer's
    tiles, rows and column types. One shared core (per-tile row order, tile
    layout, parquet writer) with one module per input format: parquet
    (Xenium, Atera preview, MERSCOPE, bin points) and zarr (Atera v1). The
    tile plan stays tilework's own; only its counting moves to Rust.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
